WEBVTT

00:00:13.741 --> 00:00:14.552
The portal's new look.

00:00:15.755 --> 00:00:17.547
The payments portal is where we manage the

00:00:17.589 --> 00:00:18.289
orchestrator.

00:00:18.656 --> 00:00:19.979
This is a sample of a new look

00:00:20.064 --> 00:00:20.641
for it.

00:00:20.661 --> 00:00:21.429
The functions stay.

00:00:22.069 --> 00:00:24.331
The look changes, for finance teams and

00:00:24.459 --> 00:00:25.696
anyone who is not a developer.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:30.139
Today, the dashboard opens on eleven equal tiles.

00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:32.358
The sample opens on three.

00:00:34.494 --> 00:00:35.603
First, one glance.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.395
Green for payments collected,

00:00:37.864 --> 00:00:39.187
amber for payments to follow up,

00:00:39.528 --> 00:00:40.723
red for processor errors.

00:00:42.037 --> 00:00:43.360
Each card carries its count,

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:45.024
and a link to the next step.

00:00:47.268 --> 00:00:48.889
Second, numbers that add up.

00:00:49.273 --> 00:00:50.937
Four hundred and ten payments were

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.241
started, and each one lands in one of

00:00:53.284 --> 00:00:54.009
five outcomes:

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:57.209
paid, bank declined, processor error,

00:00:57.679 --> 00:00:58.575
stopped at the bank check,

00:00:58.831 --> 00:00:59.727
or checkout unfinished.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:02.884
The approval rate says what it counts:

00:01:03.353 --> 00:01:05.529
forty-one paid, out of forty-eight that

00:01:05.572 --> 00:01:07.108
were paid or declined by a bank.

00:01:07.748 --> 00:01:09.198
Processor errors are kept apart.

00:01:11.423 --> 00:01:13.727
Third, one payment in plain words.

00:01:14.196 --> 00:01:16.415
Pick an outcome, and the list narrows to it.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:19.334
Open a payment, and it says what happened:

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.766
a processor error, two tries,

00:01:22.321 --> 00:01:23.345
the processor's own answer,

00:01:23.814 --> 00:01:24.838
and whether to retry.

00:01:25.478 --> 00:01:26.178
Nothing was taken.

00:01:28.393 --> 00:01:29.758
Fourth, where payments go.

00:01:30.228 --> 00:01:32.105
Routing rules are written as sentences.

00:01:32.745 --> 00:01:35.347
In Canada, cards split fifty fifty between

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:37.395
two processor accounts, and if one

00:01:37.438 --> 00:01:38.889
refuses, the other is tried.

00:01:40.255 --> 00:01:41.791
To change it, move the slider,

00:01:42.175 --> 00:01:43.753
say why, and request a review.

00:01:44.351 --> 00:01:46.825
No payment changes until another admin approves.

00:01:49.147 --> 00:01:51.366
Fifth, one page, four ways.

00:01:52.134 --> 00:01:53.840
Statement, for totals that add up.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:56.144
Traffic lights, for status at a glance.

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:58.150
Briefing, in plain English.

00:01:58.747 --> 00:02:01.179
Workbook, in rows and columns for Finance.

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:04.621
And each one comes in light or dark.

00:02:06.263 --> 00:02:07.031
That is the sample:

00:02:07.415 --> 00:02:08.994
eleven pages, four looks,

00:02:09.591 --> 00:02:11.170
built from the portal's own test data.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:13.474
It is a proposal, not yet built.

00:02:13.986 --> 00:02:16.050
So, which look do you want to work in?

